<title>USA: Cousins properties makes $20.1 mln sale.</title>
<headline>Cousins properties makes $20.1 mln sale.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cousins Properties Inc, a publically traded real estate investment trust, said on Wednesday that it sold two Atlanta neighborhood shopping centers to Regency Realty Corporation for $20.l million through its affiliate, Cousins Real Estate Corporation.</p>
<p>In a statement, Cousins said it sold the Rivermont Station and Lovejoy Station centers.</p>
<p>The Rivermont Station, completed in 1996, is a 90,000 square foot center located in north Fulton County.  The Lovejoy Station, completed in 1995, is a 77,000 square foot center located in Clayton County.</p>
</text>
